<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nestor</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nestor of Pylos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nestor is a legendary king of Pylos in Greek mythology, son of Neleus. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iliad">Iliad</a> he is the oldest of the Greek leaders at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Troy</a>, a wise counsellor fond of recalling his youthful deeds, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odyssey">Odyssey</a> he receives Telemachus at Pylos. The Mycenaean palace discovered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carl-blegen">Carl Blegen</a> at Pylos in 1939 is known as the Palace of Nestor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nestor.jpg" alt="Nestor" width="320" height="316" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Briseis_Phoinix_Louvre_G152.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
